---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import {REPO,topics} from '../../scripts/catalog.mjs';
---
<Layout title="Contribute · Aha Looped Transformer"><div class="paper-page"><div class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span>Community contributions</div><h1 style="margin-top:14px">One paper.<br/><em>Another perspective.</em></h1><p class="paper-lede">Help researchers find the next idea in recurrent computation. Add a work, share its implementation, or improve an existing entry.</p><ol class="workflow"><li data-family="core">01 · Submit a paper</li><li data-family="adaptive">02 · Metadata checks</li><li data-family="full">03 · Maintainer review</li><li data-family="core">04 · Published automatically</li></ol><div class="panel"><h2>Share a work</h2><p>Bring an arXiv link, a short description in your own words, and any official code or weights. Sign in to GitHub to submit the form. The bot prepares the entry and a review link. A maintainer checks the sources, adds topic tags, and merges a pull request before publication.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href={`${REPO}/issues/new?template=submit-paper.yml`}>Open submission form ↗</a><a class="gh-button" href={`${REPO}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`}>Contribute with a pull request ↗</a></div></div><section class="block"><h2>What belongs here?</h2><p>Research on shared computation across depth, recurrent Transformer cores, adaptive recursion, and related latent reasoning methods. Include a source that explains the connection. Classifications can overlap; maintainers select the primary browsing category and up to four topics: {Object.values(topics).join(', ')}.</p><p>Use precise claims: independent parameters, effective depth and actual latency describe different things. Indicate unknown details and distinguish official releases from community implementations.</p></section><p class="muted">Submissions with missing metadata remain in review. Corrected and merged entries appear automatically on the collection, timeline, comparison view and their own paper page.</p></div></Layout>
